---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Heading from '../Heading.astro';
---

<Section id="faq" labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 xl:grid-cols-[400px_minmax(0,1fr)] xl:gap-20">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
      <Heading id="faq-title">Common questions</Heading>
      <p class="text-[17px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2">
        Practical details people ask before trying Kix.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="border-t-[1.5px] border-ink">
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Is Kix open source?</dt>
        <dd>
          Yes. Kix, including the Rust compiler CLI, the Nix library, and the package catalog, is open source under the
          Apache 2.0 license on <a
            href="https://github.com/kix-run/kix"
            class="font-medium text-accent-text hover:underline">GitHub</a
          >.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Is it still standard Kubernetes underneath?</dt>
        <dd>
          Yes. Kix outputs ordinary Kubernetes resources that kubectl, dashboards, operators, and security tools can
          inspect.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>What if I stop using Kix?</dt>
        <dd>
          <code class="rounded bg-paper-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[14px] text-ink">kix export</code> writes your
          cluster out as plain Kubernetes YAML that you can keep managing with standard tools.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Can I adopt Kix gradually on an existing cluster?</dt>
        <dd>
          Yes. Kix can manage a single namespace or a few applications alongside your existing Helm or GitOps setup.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Can Kix use existing Helm charts?</dt>
        <dd>
          Yes. You can import existing Helm charts directly, though native Kix packages give you deeper checks and
          automatic wiring.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>What if Kix doesn't model something I need?</dt>
        <dd>You can define any raw Kubernetes resource or field directly in your cluster definition.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Does anything need to run in my cluster?</dt>
        <dd>
          No controller runs in the cluster. Kix deploys from your laptop or CI and stores a small deployment receipt as
          a custom resource.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Does Kix block insecure configs?</dt>
        <dd>
          Security checks run on every build as warnings by default, and you can choose which rules fail the build.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-row">
        <dt>Which packages exist?</dt>
        <dd class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <span>Databases, observability, networking, routing, and common applications.</span>
          <a href="/packages" class="self-start font-semibold text-accent-text hover:underline"
            >Browse the Packages page →</a
          >
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .faq-row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-block: 22px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .faq-row {
      grid-template-columns: 340px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 40px;
    }
  }
  dt {
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  dd {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
